{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#127","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#127","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#127\",\"parent_revision\":\"5358488bdc3690213e91bc2a00aaf737abeb2cc7283d6daecbfa21194c6a8df3\",\"root_revision\":\"5358488bdc3690213e91bc2a00aaf737abeb2cc7283d6daecbfa21194c6a8df3\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`prek` downloads and pins node **26.8.1** for every `language: node` hook. That binary aborts on macOS 12:\\n\\n```\\ndyld: Symbol not found: (__ZNSt3__122__libcpp_verbose_abortEPKcz)\\nReferenced from: ~/.cache/prek/tools/node/26.8.1/bin/node\\nExpected in: /usr/lib/libc++.1.dylib\\n```\\n\\n`language_version: system` does not help \u2014 prek ignores it and downloads 26.8.1 regardless, and it exposes no toolchain override.\\n</div>\\n\\n## This Is Prek Not The Hook\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nWorth stating plainly because the first two diagnoses were wrong. The `biome-check` failure looked like a biome problem; then oxlint/oxfmt looked like they might avoid it by shipping native binaries. Neither reading was right:\\n\\n- `oxlint@1.80.0 --version` and `oxfmt@0.65.0 --version` both **execute fine** on this machine.\\n- `uv run prek run oxlint --all-files` still aborts with the identical error.\\n\\nThe tool is irrelevant. Any `language: node` hook fails the same way, because prek's own node is what aborts.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Consequence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nEvery JS/TS hook is unverifiable locally on this machine. Verification falls to CI, which means a JS hook change ships unproven from the contributor's side.\\n\\nUpstream `pre-commit` honours `language_version: system` and runs the same hooks correctly \u2014 that was the workaround used to verify #126.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Options\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Ask prek upstream for a toolchain override or `language_version: system` support.\\n- Run JS hooks through `pre-commit` rather than `prek`.\\n- Accept CI-only verification for JS hooks and record it, so the next person does not spend the diagnosis again.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #126 \u2014 replaced biome with oxlint/oxfmt; verified through upstream `pre-commit` for this reason\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"0ac69a20a2c58aaf6796ba5ece6a72ecd03fbdbd266ad494f6d23cce7d4ee7f4\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABXP-aPw\"}"}